---
description: Applyr job-application drafting/review. Use when drafting, reviewing, or verifying a resume or cover letter for a job application in this repo (data/submissions/), or when given a job description to evaluate for fit.
alwaysApply: false
---

This repo has a mandatory, already-written process for this. Do not draft, evaluate fit, or
invent your own structure from general resume-writing instinct -- read the real files first,
in this order:

1. Read `AGENTS.md` (repo root) in full. It owns the hard rules -- anti-hallucination, forbidden
   language, PII/exclusion zones, the required document structure and 1-page rule. Verified
   metrics and approved accomplishments (MET-*/ACC-*) live in `data/workExperience.md`, not here.
2. Read `.claude/skills/generate-submission/SKILL.md` in full. It owns the actual sequence.
   **Canonical entry point is `python scripts/run_submission.py data/submissions/{slug}`**
   (CR-076–084): Stage 0 → packet/prompt → WAITING_FOR_LLM → Stage 1 validate → Truth/ATS/HM/
   Mech/Policy → optional `--finalize`. Under the hood it still uses CR-074 workers; do not
   call those as the default sequencing path. Do not load `agent_context_pack.md` into the
   Stage 1 author session. Follow the skill literally.
3. No web search for the Stage 0 fit decision. Stage 1 may use the narrow hook-fact exception
   documented in the skill (Tier 1 / Reach Out only). Every claim traces to packet excerpts /
   `data/workExperience.md` / `data/master_claims_tags_only.json` (tags only) /
   `data/conversion_rubric.md` / `data/candidate_preferences.json`.
4. Before reporting any submission as done, run the commands in `SKILL.md`'s "Required
   Verification (before reporting any real submission done)" section and show the real output,
   not a summary. Done means workflow `COMPLETE` / `COMPLETE_WITH_OVERRIDE` (or
   `PRACTICE_COMPLETE` in practice), with dispositions settled and `check_workflow_complete` YES
   for production. Workers are debug-only -- if you run them by hand, still finish with
   `--resume` so `workflow_state` + `stage_receipts` stay authoritative.
5. If anything is ambiguous -- a fit call you can't resolve from the JD text, a gap with no
   honest bridge, a blocked-industry judgment call -- stop and ask. Do not guess and do not
   search the web to resolve it.

Do not restate or duplicate the rules from `AGENTS.md`/`SKILL.md` into this file or into any
other file -- if a rule here ever needs to change, it changes there, not here. This file is a
pointer, nothing else.
